WEBVTT

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.660
Robby, thank you for coming.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.160
This is a surprise, you coming to me.
What brings you here?

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.910
Uh, right. Um, you see,

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.250
I was actually wondering if I could
get some additional financing.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.790
Do you realize how much
debt you already have?!

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.200
Are you an idiot?!

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.620
Now, now...

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.750
--Y-Yes, sir.
--Y-Yes, sir.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.120
Robby, since you're the one asking...

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.040
You mean you'll lend it to me?

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.950
But the repayment deadline
for what you already owe is near.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.910
If you can't repay me...

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.200
If I can't repay you...?

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.540
Then you'd better say your prayers.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.120
I-It's all right. This investment
is sure to pay off.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.750
I'll see dividends the
next day after I invest it,

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.450
so I can pay the previous part right away!

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.250
All right, Robby.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.290
Oh! Thank you so much!

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.120
"Milk Strawberry"
Um, would you like some?

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.290
Huh? For me?

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:29.040
Well, I didn't want to come
empty-handed, so I brought these.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.700
S-Since you went to the trouble, I'll take them.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.370
Oh, well, I stopped at a pachinko
parlor on the way here, is all.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:40.120
I'm glad you like them, though.
Okay, I promise I'll pay you back in time.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.120
I'll be expecting you, Robby.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.080
Right, Mr. Yang.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.830
Why is Mr. Yang so hell-bent
on chasing after Robby?

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:01.160
Who knows? Maybe to make
an example of him

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.830
for what happens if you don't pay.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:06.870
Eek. Then Robby isn't going to get off easy.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.250
Just you wait, Robby.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.870
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:22.660
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.700
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.080
"The heartwarming road trip anime <i>RobiHachi</i>"
"Wandering down the Galaxy Highway"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.290
"The planet Odwarla is a watery world"
"Merfolk on the End of the Pole"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.950
"The planet Odwarla is a watery world"
"Merfolk on the End of the Pole"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:53.950
"The journey to Isekandar"

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:58.200
"The journey to Isekandar"
After departing Earth,
we made stops at Mars and Pluto,

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.160
"The journey to Isekandar"
but now we've warped out of the solar system!

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.040
"The journey to Isekandar"
That being said, Isekandar is still
a journey of 2,290,000 light years,

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.200
"53 stage station planets"
That being said, Isekandar is still
a journey of 2,290,000 light years,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.290
"53 stage station planets"
and we first have to head
to the Haccone checkpoint,

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.500
"53 stage station planets"
doorway to the rest of the universe!

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.000
Okay, let's keep straight on to Haccone!

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.870
Hold on. As long as we're taking a trip,
let's stop off at some stage stations.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:24.790
What for? Let's get to Isekandar quick
and get us some Akafucrystals.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:28.870
Isn't the journey all about visiting
the 53 stage station worlds?

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.870
Well, I guess there <i>is </i>that.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.950
This is strange.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.410
Hmm? What is it, Ikku?

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.370
I said this is strange.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:40.120
The same ships have been behind us
ever since we left Pluto.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.040
Are you sure they aren't Yang's ships?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.120
No, they aren't.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.830
Then maybe some cute girlies
have come chasing after me.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.620
Idiot.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.120
It is kind of creepy, so let's let them pass.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.160
Got it.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:56.660
Okay then, let's stop at a
stage station world near here!

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.160
The ocean, the ocean! This place is on fire!

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.580
Oh, and I don't mean in the "hot girl" way,
I mean in the "burning" way.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.830
If I know you, you're planning
to get busy with a girl on the beach.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.330
Of course I am. The ocean means beaches,

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.370
and beaches mean girls
while sipping cocktails.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.040
Actually, there's nothing <i>but </i>ocean here.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:27.250
Aren't there any continents?
Where are the beaches?!

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.200
This is Odwarla, otherwise known
as the "water planet."

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.330
The water planet? You mean,
there's nothing here but water?

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:37.290
It's okay, land has been artificially created

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.700
to allow people to live here...

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.950
Is that...?

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.700
--Fish loaf?
--Fish loaf?

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:55.870
These guys are Odwarlans?
They just look like merpeople to me.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.450
Originally, there were nothing
but oceans on this world,

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.660
so everyone lived in the sea.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.660
In time, artificial land was constructed,

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.660
and the Odwarlans adapted
to the environment.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.450
Oh, yeah? You know your stuff.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:11.000
I think preliminary research
is always warranted.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.040
Ah, are you the type of person
who thoroughly looks up

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.700
restaurant popularity ratings
before going out to eat?

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.660
Huh?

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:20.750
Bullseye!

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:24.200
Yeah, that's right! Assuming a life of 80 years,

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:28.450
some quick math shows that
amounts to 87,600 meals eaten.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:32.250
I've already lived 18 years,
so subtracting 19,710,

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.870
that leaves 67,890 meals to go.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:39.660
I don't want to have any crummy food
for even one of those remaining meals!

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:40.830
O-Okay...

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.660
All right, let's eat here.
They have a 4.5-star rating.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.790
Hey, hold on!

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:49.830
"Merfolk's Odwarla Specialty
Seafood Bowl Restaurant"?

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.410
Welcome!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.750
What is this?

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.700
What looks like a boat
is sticking out into the sea.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.290
Our seafood bowl is the
"Self-Seafood Bowl," a local specialty

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.540
that you catch yourself!

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:05.200
Oh, yeah? We catch the seafood
that goes in it for ourselves?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.250
Hey, you two.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.040
Hurry! Hurry! Let's start fishing!

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.160
Why is he always so up for anything?

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.250
Haven't we caught anything yet? I'm starving.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:18.580
I'm tired of this, too.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.410
Already? It hasn't even been five minutes yet.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:25.700
I don't even eat fish. All I really
need is a power outlet.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:27.700
What is it?!

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.750
I got a bite! Wh-What do I do, Robby?

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.080
Haven't you ever gone fishing before?

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.580
Whoa, it's pulling the line!

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.540
Here, give me that!

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:37.330
You keep the rod at the same angle,

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:41.080
and when the pulling gets weaker,
you reel in the line.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:44.620
Wow!

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:46.910
What kind of nasty fish is that?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:50.000
Awesome! I've never seen
a fish like this before!

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.620
That is an Odwarla-uo.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:54.410
It's one of our best specialties.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:56.910
Would you like it <i>donburi </i>style?
Or perhaps as sashimi?

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.790
Two <i>donburi</i>-styles, please.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.830
Very good, sir.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.580
Thank you for waiting!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.200
Wow! I've never seen something
so colorful and goopy before!

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.000
Thank you for this food!

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:15.370
Is he for real?

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.250
What's up with this weird stickiness?

00:08:17.250 --> 00:08:21.290
Ugh, I've lost my appetite.
But I'm still hungry.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:25.790
Go on, eat up, eat up! We may never
come here in our lifetimes again.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.540
Ah, what the hell. Here goes nothing!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.200
That was delicious!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.200
Okay, that will be 1200 mons.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.500
I'm sorry, but I'm actually out of money!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.330
Huh? How come?! Your money
is what I was counting on!

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.120
This will not do, sir.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:50.620
So now, if I could ask a favor,

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:53.660
your restaurant is looking
for part-time workers, right?

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:56.080
Can we work off what we owe?

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.200
Oh, well, that's another matter entirely.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.700
The labor reforms of late
have left us undermanned--

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.660
or rather, under-mermanned,
and we're at our wit's end.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.410
We'll even take robot help if we can get it.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.660
Then please, allow all
three of us to work for you.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.450
How come you get to decide for all of us?

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.200
Count me out of working in a place like this!

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.750
Back on Mars, you seemed
to be pretty well off,

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:22.120
so I was pinning my hopes on you.
And now, you're... you're...

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.290
Hey, Robby...

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.040
Hey, are you all right?

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.370
Robby!

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.750
Food poisoning?

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.660
Has he eaten a great deal
of cold foods recently?

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:42.540
Oh, he may have eaten a lot
of shave ice back on Pluto.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:47.700
Ah, that must be it. Well, let's keep him
here overnight for observation.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.330
Very well. Thank you, Doctor.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.040
Okay, I wanna hear you in high spirits today!

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.250
Welcome!

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.870
--Welcome!
--Welcome.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:01.540
Thank you!

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.080
--Thank you!
--Thank you.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.410
Wait, this is just wrong, isn't it?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.160
How did we allow ourselves
to work at this restaurant?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:13.910
I'd be happy to!

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:18.540
Welcome!

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:20.160
Thank you!

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.200
--Thank you!
--It's hopeless. He's enjoying this.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:29.950
Huh? Where am I?

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:31.080
Y-Yes?

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.450
I'm here to change your IV.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.500
How are you feeling?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.410
Ah, it's you!

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.290
When I was hospitalized two years ago

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.540
after falling down the stairs
at the <i>nata de coco </i>plant,

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.000
you were my pretty nurse!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:45.660
Long time no see.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:55.950
It was a cold day,
and a chilling rain was falling...

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:41.370
Be a man and pay more
attention to your appearance.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:59.870
Come with me. I'll buy you something to eat.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:17.200
It was a summer day, and the
sunlight shined down warmly...

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:03.250
Be a man and pay more
attention to your appearance.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:08.500
Huh?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.620
Be a man and pay more
attention to your appearance.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.000
Huh? What was that?

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:21.250
Be a man! And pay more attention!
To your appearance!

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.500
Huh? What are you saying?

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:31.700
Be! A! Man! And! Pay! More!
Attention! To! Your! Appearance!

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.250
I can't tell a thing you're saying.

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:36.500
Never mind!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:41.500
Come with me. I'll buy you something to eat.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.040
Long time no see.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.700
What are you doing here?
It was a hell of a scene back there.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.790
I got chased around by those scary guys!

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:07.040
I'm sorry. Afterward, his wife
found out about me, too.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:10.750
I can't stay on Earth anymore,
so I came home to Odwarla.

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.660
I-Is that right?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:17.500
But I never thought
I'd run into you again here.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.160
I'm sure this must be destiny.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:31.450
That's awesome, all right.
Washing with not a sponge, but webbing!

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:33.870
Hey, Gyo-Gyo, let me see, let me see!

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.410
Yeah, sure, whatever.

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:39.290
Wow! I'll bet you're fast when you swim, too.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:42.370
You might say that. We used
to live in the ocean, after all.

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:45.040
So, how do you breathe now?

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:48.410
We breathe with lungs now,
though we can breathe with gills, too.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:52.250
Awesome! You can change
depending on your location!

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:57.500
But we've lived on land for so long,
our gills have atrophied quite a bit.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:02.790
So my goal is to work hard here, save up
some money, and buy an undersea suit.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.160
So you want to return to the sea?

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.830
No, life on land isn't so bad.

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.540
I just want to catch an elusive fish
that lives in the seas here--

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:14.290
the Odwarla oarfish!

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:16.410
Elusive fish?

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.450
The Odwarla oarfish?

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:24.580
Yes. When you offer a fish loaf made
from this fish to the Odwarlan god,

00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:28.290
you can get all sorts of
reward money from Odwarla.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:29.870
Reward money?!

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:35.120
It's a real jackpot. But there's
something you'll need to obtain it.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.500
I want to catch an Odwarla oarfish

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.700
and throw a nice wedding
ceremony for my girl.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.120
We still haven't gone through
with the ceremony.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.160
An Odwarla oarfish, huh?

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:50.660
I kind of want him to catch one, myself.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:51.790
Yeah.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.830
I wonder if merfolk also wear
rings when they get married.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.410
Can you even wear a ring
when your fingers are webbed?

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:59.830
<i>That's </i>what you're concerned about?

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.750
Okay, I wanna hear you in high spirits today!

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:03.120
Welcome!

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:06.120
--Welcome!
--Welcome!
--Jeez, he's enjoying himself today, too.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:08.700
Hey, Hatchi! Ikku!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.870
Quit working, already, and let's go!

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:13.540
Huh? Robby? What do you mean? Go where?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.660
Wait, what are you doing out of the hospital?

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.750
To catch an Odwarla oarfish, of course!

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:20.750
I have all the gear ready, too.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:21.950
Fishing gear?

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:27.120
Not just any fishing gear. It's the
Odwarla oarfish premium hunting set.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.750
As it happens...

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:36.410
You dumbass! Did that pretty
nurse set you up again?!

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.250
Let's do it. It sounds like fun.

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:39.120
Huh?

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.370
We'll earn a whole bunch
of reward money, too.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.250
You knew about this, too?
Well, that speeds things along.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.540
Let's go catch one and hit the jackpot!

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.450
Together with Gyo-Gyo.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.700
Gyo?

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.200
Uh... Gyo?

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:56.330
Damn it, not a single bite.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.750
Isn't it odd that in our modern times,
with our advanced technology,

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.330
we're going about this in such a primitive way?

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:05.540
But that pretty nurse made
him buy this whole set.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.000
Shut up! Don't diss the premium set!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.580
Ugh, these fish are all gross.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:16.700
Awesome! How colorful!
It's like a treasure chest of fish!

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.910
There aren't any Odwarla oarfish, though.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.200
Good-for-nothing premium set.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.290
Damn it! This calls for...

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.410
Galaxy Traveler Hizakuriger!

00:17:54.370 --> 00:18:02.000
Hizakuriger!

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.120
Okay, so we're combined. Now what?

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.660
We dive into the sea and
catch an Odwarla oarfish.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:11.040
Let's go!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:24.120
By the way, should they have
really gone underwater like that?

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.370
Gyo-Gyo?

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:39.250
Come on, where the hell
are you, Odwarla oarfish?

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:44.290
Hey, something's creaking. I don't think
this robot is all that waterproof.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.290
Don't be ridiculous. How can something
that does fine in outer space

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:48.660
not do fine in the water?

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:50.080
Outer space has zero atmospheres;

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.290
that's not much different from
the one atmosphere at sea level.

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:54.040
But for every ten meters
we go under the water,

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:56.750
it adds another atmosphere of pressure,
so 100 meters under the water

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:59.750
is like ten times the difference
in atmospheric pressure of space...

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:01.080
There, you see?

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.790
"There, you see?" Why didn't you
say something sooner?

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.160
Oh, crap!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.790
We're retreating upward!

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.660
What is with this rickety old robot?
Is it all hollow? How shoddy!

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:15.950
You can tell by watching it transform, right?
This robot is mostly empty.

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.250
There's probably an escape hatch up top.

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:25.450
Will we make it in time?

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:27.290
Yeah, that's a good question.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.620
What's going to become of us?

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:33.290
Whatever happens, happens. Just hurry!

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:43.620
Was this outcome within your predictions?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:46.250
Well, this possibility did exist.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.620
You're just as tedious as ever.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.950
Tedious or not, it'll all be over if we're dead.

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.500
Yeah, well...

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:58.080
Found the way out!

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:59.290
Hurry!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:29.700
Whew, that was a close one.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:32.830
But we didn't catch anything.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.450
What's the use? Money, women,

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:38.040
and that thrilling, heart-pounding
sensation of being alive?

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:40.250
Doesn't mean a thing if you're dead.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:44.700
He's right, Hatchi. Just be glad you're alive.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:48.700
Besides, the three of us are
all going to Isekandar, right?

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:52.790
But... Hizakuriger is a mess now,
and what's more...

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:57.750
Oh, that's okay. Thanks to you,
I've discovered by swimming in the sea

00:20:57.750 --> 00:21:03.160
that my atrophied gills will work
just fine with a little training.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.120
In fact, I'd like to thank <i>you</i>!

00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:09.580
No, no, you're the one who bailed <i>us </i>out.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:11.000
What's that?

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:15.700
I-Is that...?

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.790
An Odwarla oarfish!

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:30.040
All's well that ends well.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:37.040
At last, we can kiss this planet goodbye.

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:40.870
Yeah. And we picked up the reward
money for the Odwarla oarfish.

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:43.330
But half of it went to pay for
that whatever-it's-called set

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:46.080
from Robby's pretty nurse,

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:49.410
and half of the rest went
to Gyo-Gyo's wedding gift.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.750
And another half went to pay for
craning Hizakuriger out of the sea.

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:55.200
There's hardly any left.

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:59.450
Now, now, say what you will,
but it's enough for our expenses for now.

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.500
All thanks to me.

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.620
How the hell can you claim that?!

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:10.040
Still, I really am glad that Gyo-Gyo
could have his wedding. Here,

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:12.660
look at this wedding reception mug of them.

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:15.910
Odwarla sure has been a lot of fun, huh?

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:20.580
Yeah. The food and the wedding
souvenirs were iffy, though.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:53.080
"Next time"
"#05 'The Don Opens All Doors'"

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:57.200
"Next time"
"#05 'The Don Opens All Doors'"
Next time, "The Don Opens All Doors."

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:01.910
"Haccone, exit point of the galaxy"
"But you need a pass to go through?"

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:06.910
"In order to get their passes,"
"they have to find the don of Haccone!"
